From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Desidero <desidero@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 18:31:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(routing): route only the sub-agents of a native session

A common setup is a strong coordinator on a model the user chose, with
cheaper models picked per task for the sub-agents it starts. On a native
Claude Code or Codex session that was not possible: the gate that routes
the CLI's own sub-agents (Claude Code's Agent/Task, Codex's spawn_agent)
is installed at launch, and only for a session launched on Smart
Routing, which also routes the coordinator's model.

A create that asks for `subagent_routing_override: "on"` on a native
Claude Code or Codex session now stamps the label
`omnigent.routing.subagent_routing`. Every launch of such a session
installs the spawn-routing endpoint and hook (on Codex also the
routed-spawn tool approvals and the extended model catalog), and nothing
that touches the session's own model: no first-message hook, no alias or
launch-model pins. The label, not the switch, is what launches read,
because the switch can change mid-session and the gate cannot be added
afterwards. The switch is still read per spawn, so it turns routing of
later spawns off and on.

The new-session composer offers "Route sub-agents" under Smart Routing
when a Claude Code or Codex model is picked, and the session's model
menu has the same row. A native session created without it, whose switch
is turned on later through the API, routes its Omnigent child sessions
only, as before; the row then says so. The family rule is unchanged:
spawns stay in the session's model family, and sys_agent_list is
confined accordingly.

A create with a bound inference profile now refuses the switch, as
PATCH already did: nothing on the routing paths consults the profile's
model list, and the launch gate would otherwise route such a session's
spawns.

Not upstream yet: tracked by issue https://github.com/omnigent-ai/omnigent/issues/14897;
not proposed as a pull request yet. Drop this copy once it merges.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Desidero <desidero@gmail.com>
